The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
rc = bnxt_qplib_free_mrw(&rdev->qplib_res, &mr->qplib_mr);
if (rc) {
    ...
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the driver attempts to free the memory region (MR) structure even when the deregistration of the MR fails (indicated by a non-zero return code `rc`). This leads to the MR structure being accessed again after it has been freed, resulting in a NULL pointer dereference and a system crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (rc) {
    dev_err(rdev_to_dev(rdev), "Dereg MR failed: %#x\n", rc);
    return rc;
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves adding a return statement when the deregistration fails, preventing the subsequent code from executing that would free the MR structure. This ensures that the MR structure remains valid and is not accessed after being freed, thus avoiding the NULL pointer dereference and potential system crash.

